# Commit and push

When the work for a request is done, create a git commit and push to the tracked remote. Do not wait for a separate "commit" or "push" request.

- Follow the existing commit protocol: status, diff, log, HEREDOC message, no secrets, no `--no-verify`, no force push to main unless explicitly requested.
- Push the current branch (`git push`, or `git push -u origin HEAD` if it has no upstream).
- If there is nothing to commit, skip the commit. Still push if the branch is ahead of origin.
